					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-474634#post-1483344</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-474634/a-world-we-live-in#post-1483344</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 18 Jun 2012 19:15:21 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>wishun</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1204404</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>It's a great idea, &quot;scp-eople&quot; who are otherwise just regular folk is pretty existentially creepy; and I really like the toss-off guard. There might be enough meat in that idea to make a good item. You'd have to find the right spin on his psychology and world-view to make it truly interesting, but it could be done and done well.<br /> But something about this just leaves me flat. Maybe it's too short to really cement the mood in my mind? Sorry I can't pin it down, but I'm left with just a lot of meh. Which is too bad, because I want to like it.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
